From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000038 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliphaunt Maintainers <dev@oliphaunt.dev>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] oliphaunt-wasix: disable unsupported writeback hints

PostgreSQL uses pg_flush_data() as an optional asynchronous writeback hint.
During startup it opens every data file read-only before issuing that hint.
WASIX exposes posix_fadvise(), but its descriptor-capability implementation
rejects the operation on those read-only descriptors with EACCES. PostgreSQL
promotes the otherwise ignorable hint failure to PANIC during recovery.

Do not advertise pg_flush_data() for the explicitly single-backend WASIX
build. Real durability remains provided by PostgreSQL's fsync/fdatasync calls;
only the unsupported pre-writeback optimization is disabled. Other PostgreSQL
targets retain the upstream selection logic.
---
 src/backend/storage/file/fd.c | 7 ++++++-
 src/common/file_utils.c       | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/storage/file/fd.c b/src/backend/storage/file/fd.c
index 739b1b9..b1f0a22 100644
--- a/src/backend/storage/file/fd.c
+++ b/src/backend/storage/file/fd.c
@@ -103,7 +103,12 @@
 #include "utils/varlena.h"
 
 /* Define PG_FLUSH_DATA_WORKS if we have an implementation for pg_flush_data */
-#if defined(HAVE_SYNC_FILE_RANGE)
+#if defined(OLIPHAUNT_WASM_SINGLE_USER)
+/*
+ * WASIX rejects the startup pre-sync hint on PostgreSQL's read-only file
+ * descriptors.  Actual fsync/fdatasync durability remains enabled.
+ */
+#elif defined(HAVE_SYNC_FILE_RANGE)
 #define PG_FLUSH_DATA_WORKS 1
 #elif !defined(WIN32) && defined(MS_ASYNC)
 #define PG_FLUSH_DATA_WORKS 1
diff --git a/src/common/file_utils.c b/src/common/file_utils.c
index d0ddfd9..066d455 100644
--- a/src/common/file_utils.c
+++ b/src/common/file_utils.c
@@ -34,7 +34,12 @@
 #include "common/logging.h"
 
 /* Define PG_FLUSH_DATA_WORKS if we have an implementation for pg_flush_data */
-#if defined(HAVE_SYNC_FILE_RANGE)
+#if defined(OLIPHAUNT_WASM_SINGLE_USER)
+/*
+ * WASIX rejects the startup pre-sync hint on PostgreSQL's read-only file
+ * descriptors.  Actual fsync/fdatasync durability remains enabled.
+ */
+#elif defined(HAVE_SYNC_FILE_RANGE)
 #define PG_FLUSH_DATA_WORKS 1
 #elif !defined(WIN32) && defined(MS_ASYNC)
 #define PG_FLUSH_DATA_WORKS 1
